<!--
  kuna: a `type` directive retyping a register local to a pointer to a structure declared
  without a body. `probe` keeps &frame[1] of a stack array in a saved register (ARM32
  little-endian `int *v1; // r4`, PowerPC32 big-endian `int *v2; // r29`) and passes it
  to four calls.
  Stage: P6 frame layout under the stable-names replay (`funcdata_spacebase.rs`
  gather_open, `kuna_stablenames.rs` holds_retype).
  P0 assertion: the `retype` directive; the fix is always on, no option.
  The locked pointer's size-0 pointee added a default one-byte range that split the
  array, the copy holding the address was propagated away and the retype refused, with
  `int4 *v3` printed in its place (`nothing is declared as v1 after it`). One pass per
  byte order pins the fixed declaration and its cast, the four uses in each listing, and
  the unchanged stack array; asserts 1-3 and 5-7 fail without the fix.
-->
<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="ARM:LE:32:v8:default">
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">1eff2fe1</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
